# The scene after kind $73's chain is beaten in level $11 ($84:8B08 on, in
# the last piece, $40 = 8): the pieces' children and tasks started, the
# fade waited on, the head moved off and the closing lists, then TaskExec
# to what follows. Each pass plays cov_kind73_defeat.box's second pass
# (the head's health, $11 at $0C0C, set to 0 before the strike).
# Pass 1 waits through the whole scene to TaskExec $80:AF42 ($005D 0).
# Pass 2 sets the player's health ($0367) to 0 twenty frames after the
# strike: the piece then waits in the $84:8B4A loop (measured from frame
# 20 to 660 after the strike, $0087 clear by 680), so its read at $84:8B64
# finds 0 and it stays for good ($84:8B69).
# Not covered: $84:8CA1 (TaskExec $84:AFCC, 7 bytes), taken only with
# $005D nonzero, which RegionCheck ($84:AFAE) sets only on a PAL console
# (STAT78 bit 4); this board is NTSC.
